<Base title="Terms of Service | CQLocalPal" description="The plain-language terms behind every CQLocalPal booking: what we promise, what we don't, and how disagreements get solved.">
  <section>
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="muted small">Last updated: 4 November 2026 · v1.0</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>CQLocalPal provides local assistance services in Chongqing, China: arrival welcomes, remote concierge support, guided private days and food experiences. Bookings are confirmed individually in writing (WhatsApp or email) before any payment.</p>
        <h2>2. Prices and payment</h2>
        <p>All prices are in Chinese yuan (CNY), fixed per service as listed on this site, and confirmed in writing before you pay. A deposit of ¥100 per order reserves a date; the balance is due after the service by Alipay, WeChat Pay or cash. Online card payment is introduced only once our payment approval is complete — we will never improvise a payment method outside the confirmed channels.</p>
        <h2>3. Your responsibilities</h2>
        <p>Give us accurate arrival details, tell us about kids, allergies or mobility needs before booking, and carry valid travel documents and insurance. Costs of meals, SIM top-ups, transport fares and attraction tickets are yours unless the written confirmation says otherwise.</p>
        <h2>4. Cancellations and refunds</h2>
        <p>Governed by our <a href="/en/legal/refunds/">refund policy</a>: the 30-minute guarantee, free cancellation 48+ hours ahead, and the deposit rule inside 48 hours.</p>
        <h2>5. No-shopping rule</h2>
        <p>Our <a href="/en/legal/no-shopping/">no-shopping promise</a> is a term of every booking. If any team member steers you to a shop for commission, the service is free and we want to know.</p>
        <h2>6. Liability</h2>
        <p>We arrange and perform services with reasonable care. We are not liable for losses caused by events outside our control (flight disruptions, closures, weather) or by third-party providers beyond our reasonable selection duty. Travel insurance is your friend — we recommend it for any China trip.</p>
        <h2>7. Governing approach</h2>
        <p>We resolve disagreements by talking first: message us and a founder replies. The services are performed in Chongqing, China, and these terms follow the law of the place where the service is performed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
